---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
import t from '../../i18n/en.json';
---

<Layout t={t}>
  <Nav t={t} />
  <div class="legal-page">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-date">Last updated: October 2026</p>

      <div class="legal-body">

        <p class="legal-note">This is an English translation for convenience. The service is directed exclusively at businesses (Unternehmer within the meaning of § 14 BGB). In case of any discrepancy, the <a href="/de/privacy">German version</a> prevails.</p>

        <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
        <p>Data Controller under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR):<br/>
        <strong>Igor Zelikovsky</strong><br/>
        Digitalkin AI (trade name)<br/>
        Bleicherfeldstraße 31, 33689 Bielefeld, Germany<br/>
        Email: <a href="mailto:contact@digitalkin.co">contact@digitalkin.co</a></p>

        <h2>2. Hosting and Server Log Files</h2>
        <p>This website is hosted by Vercel Inc. (340 S Lemon Ave #4133, Walnut, CA 91789, USA). When the pages are accessed, the server automatically processes technically necessary data (including IP address, date and time of access, page accessed, browser type). The legal basis is our legitimate interest in the secure and stable operation of the website (Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR). Any transfer to the USA is based on the EU Standard Contractual Clauses. Fonts are served locally from our own server; no external font services (e.g. Google Fonts) are embedded.</p>

        <h2>3. Language Detection (Geolocation)</h2>
        <p>To select the appropriate language version, our server evaluates the country code provided by the hosting infrastructure, which is derived from your IP address. Only the country code is processed; the IP address is not stored in this context. Your language choice is stored solely in your browser (localStorage) and is not transmitted to us. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in a user-friendly presentation (Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR).</p>

        <h2>4. Analytics (Vercel Analytics)</h2>
        <p>We use Vercel Analytics for anonymous, aggregated analysis of site usage. No cookies are set and no profiles of individual visitors are created; the data collected does not allow any conclusions to be drawn about your identity. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in the statistical evaluation and improvement of our offering (Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR).</p>

        <h2>5. Contact Form</h2>
        <p>If you complete the contact form, we process the data you provide (name, email address, and optionally company and message) in order to handle your enquiry. For immediate notification, these details are forwarded to us via the messaging service Telegram (Telegram FZ-LLC, Dubai, United Arab Emirates). There is no EU Commission adequacy decision for the UAE; the transfer therefore takes place on the basis of your enquiry and for the performance of pre-contractual measures. The legal basis is Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b and lit. f GDPR. If you wish to avoid this transfer, please contact us directly by email.</p>

        <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>Personal data is deleted as soon as the purpose of processing no longer applies or statutory retention periods expire. Enquiries submitted via the contact form are deleted once they have been fully processed, unless statutory retention obligations apply.</p>

        <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
        <p>This website does not set any tracking or marketing cookies and does not embed any cookie-based analytics tool. Your language choice is stored solely in your browser's local storage (localStorage); this is not a cookie and the value is not transmitted to us.</p>

        <h2>8. Data Security</h2>
        <p>Transmission is encrypted via SSL/TLS. We apply security measures in line with the current state of the art.</p>

        <h2>9. Prizma platform: data from Facebook and Instagram</h2>
        <p>Businesses can connect their Facebook Page or Instagram professional account to the Prizma platform (app.prizma.to). For the people who comment on or write to such an account, the business is the controller. We process their data on its behalf as a processor (Art. 28 GDPR).</p>
        <p><strong>What we process:</strong> public comments on the business's posts (text, time, name or username of the author, platform IDs); messages that people send to the business in Messenger or Instagram Direct, including any name and phone number written in them; the access token the business grants when it connects its account.</p>
        <p><strong>Why:</strong> to show comments and messages to the business in Prizma; to send replies on its behalf, for example a request for a phone number; to recognise whether a comment or message is an enquiry; to create that enquiry, with the contact details and the message, in the business's own CRM.</p>
        <p>We do not use this data for advertising, do not sell it and do not use it to train AI models.</p>
        <p><strong>Service providers:</strong> the data is stored on servers of Hetzner Online GmbH in Germany. To recognise whether a comment or message is an enquiry, its text is sent to DeepSeek (Hangzhou, China). If DeepSeek does not respond, the text is sent to OpenAI (USA) instead. No adequacy decision of the EU Commission exists for China.</p>
        <p><strong>Retention:</strong> as long as the business uses the module. When the business has us disconnect its account or removes our app in its Facebook or Instagram settings, the comments, messages and tokens of that account are deleted automatically within 30 days. Enquiries already created in the business's CRM are kept by the business under its own rules.</p>
        <p><strong>Deletion:</strong> anyone can ask us to delete their data, see <a href="/en/data-deletion">Data deletion</a>.</p>

        <h2>10. Your Rights under GDPR</h2>
        <p>You have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Request access to your personal data (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Request correction of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Request erasure of your data (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Restriction of processing and data portability (Art. 18, 20 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Object to processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To exercise your rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@digitalkin.co">contact@digitalkin.co</a></p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <Footer t={t} />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page { min-height: 80vh; }
  .legal-page h1 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .legal-date { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 60px; }
  .legal-note { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .legal-body h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .legal-body p, .legal-body ul { color: var(--text-secondary, #9CA3AF); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .legal-body ul { padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .legal-body li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .legal-body a { color: var(--purple); text-decoration: none; }
  .legal-body a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .legal-body strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
</style>
